CohomCalg -- an interface to the CohomCalg software for computing cohomology of torus invariant divisors on a toric variety
***************************************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

CohomCalg is software written by Benjamin Jurke and Thorsten Rahn (in
collaboration with Ralph Blumenhagen and Helmut Roschy) for computing the
cohomology vectors of torus invariant divisors on a (normal) toric variety (see
https://github.com/BenjaminJurke/cohomCalg for more information).

CohomCalg is an efficient and careful implementation. One limitation is that
the number of rays in the fan and the number of generators of the
Stanley-Reisner ideal of the fan must both be no larger than 64.

Here is a sample usage of this package in Macaulay2.  Let's compute the
cohomology of some divisors on a smooth Fano toric variety.

